diff --git a/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-execution-contract.md b/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-execution-contract.md
index 9d39e7ae7955f42b693c917250994f33d8ca66db..e05b14816afb470c7c7befdef3fbdbe5a6742498 100644
--- a/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-execution-contract.md
+++ b/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-execution-contract.md
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ On success, `structuredContent` is the tool's outputs keyed by output name, exac
 { "isError": false, "structuredContent": { "<output>": ... }, "content": [ { "type": "text", "text": "<message>" }, { "type": "text", "text": "<outputs as JSON>" } ] }
 ```
 
+Successful and failed execution results forward only `getFormattedResult()->getMeta()['mcp'] ?? []` as `_meta`, omitted when empty and never merged into `structuredContent` or text blocks; bridge-generated errors carry no metadata.
+
 On failure, `isError` is TRUE, the explanation is the first text block, and there is no `structuredContent`: the schema describes outputs and a failure has none. A correctable input failure (`FailureCategory::isCorrectable()`, when a tool instance exists) adds a second text block starting with `ToolApi::INPUT_SCHEMA_PREFIX` followed by `ToolDefinitionSerializer::normalizeInputSchema()` as JSON, so clients can fix their arguments without a tools/list round-trip. Access denial and runtime failures omit it; reshaping arguments cannot fix those. Requests rejected by the SDK's advertised input schema remain JSON-RPC invalid-parameters errors and never reach this method.
 
 A missing `toolId`, invalid input, denied access, a failed Tool result, or a caught `\Throwable` all produce `isError: TRUE`. Input and handle exceptions keep the input classification; other exceptions caught by the bridge are runtime failures. Failures are logged to the `mcp_server_tool_bridge` channel.
diff --git a/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-plugin-deriver.md b/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-plugin-deriver.md
index c01fe9626430ec0d771a5fa919c3a00b76750bcf..31ba22c6d1f0bb9d8b2162794b4a3daab052abdf 100644
--- a/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-plugin-deriver.md
+++ b/.ai/kenkeep/nodes/bridge/map-toolapi-plugin-deriver.md
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ It iterates `mcp_tool_config` storage and skips a config when `status()` is FALS
 
 Each derivative is keyed by the config machine name and its definition `id` is `tool_api__{config_id}`. The MCP behavior annotations derive from the Tool API tool: `readOnly` is `!operation->isModifying()` and `idempotent` is `operation->isIdempotent()` (Explain/Read/Transform are non-modifying and idempotent; Trigger/Write are neither), while `destructive` stays the tool author's explicit flag. `openWorld` and `outputSchema` are inherited from the base `ToolApi` definition.
 
+The derivative's `meta` contains only `ToolDefinition::getMeta()['mcp'] ?? []`; other consumers' metadata is excluded, and mcp_server omits `_meta` when empty.
+
 The deriver also owns the Tool API to JSON Schema conversion for the derivative's `inputSchema`.
 
 When changing this, verify the derivative id still routes through `WireSafeDerivativeDiscoveryDecorator::SEPARATOR` rather than a literal separator, since `McpToolConfig::getMcpWireName()` builds the same string independently and the two must agree.
